.page type 1 say how a name would be understood

# SYNOPSIS
*type* _NAME_...

# DESCRIPTION
`type` is a gapsh builtin. For each _NAME_ it says whether it is an alias, a function, a shell builtin or a program (with its path), in that order of precedence. The options `-p` and `-v` are accepted and ignored.

# EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 if some name was not found.

# EXAMPLES
    type ls cd ll

# SEE ALSO
command(1), which(1), alias(1)
